&lt;div id="readme" class="md"&gt;&lt;p&gt;
&lt;a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev/./web/public/afterimage-logo.png"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Femarc99%2Fpresage-dev%2FHEAD%2F.%2Fweb%2Fpublic%2Fafterimage-logo.png" alt="AFTERIMAGE Logo" width="180"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h1 class="heading-element"&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A blink is a cut, not a click. Breathe steady to hold the frame still.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/strong&gt; is a five-scene interactive visual essay navigated without touching a keyboard, powered by the &lt;strong&gt;Presage SmartSpectra Node.js SDK (&lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk@3.5.0&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;. Inspired by film editor &lt;a href="https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0004555/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Walter Murch&lt;/strong&gt;'s&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Blink_of_an_Eye_%28book%29" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the Blink of an Eye&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (the observation that a human blink punctuates one thought from the next alongside the rhythm of breathing) and the blink-driven memory storytelling of &lt;a href="https://www.imdb.com/title/tt15575678/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Before Your Eyes&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, AFTERIMAGE turns involuntary webcam signals into slow darkroom controls: where you look shifts focus across a three-panel plate, chest breathing steadiness clears optical haze and develops hidden marginalia, and every natural blink turns the page once a &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;4.2 s&lt;/code&gt; Shutter Armed&lt;/strong&gt; dwell lock clears—ending in an exportable &lt;strong&gt;Contact Sheet (&lt;code&gt;.png&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt; of your sitting.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Built as a solo submission for the &lt;a href="https://dev.to/challenges/presage-2026-11-04" rel="nofollow"&gt;Presage SmartSpectra SDK Challenge&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interactive Preview (Vercel):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://afterimage-presage.vercel.app" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://afterimage-presage.vercel.app&lt;/a&gt;…&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="gh-btn-container"&gt;&lt;a class="gh-btn" href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;View on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;MIT licensed. Tested on Windows x64 (&lt;code&gt;Node v24.9.0&lt;/code&gt;, integrated webcam &lt;code&gt;USB\VID_13D3&amp;amp;PID_5415&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;960×540 @ 30fps&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk@3.5.0&lt;/code&gt;). GitHub Actions CI runs all &lt;strong&gt;21 unit tests&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;verify-trace&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (which asserts every sitting number reported in this post against committed &lt;a href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev/blob/main/web/public/sample-trace.json" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;web/public/sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; plus SDK privacy invariants), and the production Vite build on every push:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;git clone https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev.git
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; presage-dev

npm install &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; npm --prefix web install
cp .env.example .env      &lt;span class="c"&gt;# Add SMARTSPECTRA_API_KEY=...&lt;/span&gt;
npm run check             &lt;span class="c"&gt;# 21 unit tests + verify-trace + frontend build&lt;/span&gt;
npm start                 &lt;span class="c"&gt;# Starts localhost bridge &amp;amp; UI on http://127.0.0.1:4199&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


How It Responds to Human Signals
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rather than piping raw SDK packets straight into React state, &lt;a href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev/blob/main/bridge/signal-processor.mjs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bridge/signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; transforms them into scale-invariant events. Every rule came from running it on my own laptop camera and watching what broke first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


Sitting 1 → Sitting 2 → Sitting 3: What Broke and What Fixed It
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Run&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Duration &amp;amp; Frames&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Breath Clarity&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Gaze Split (&lt;code&gt;L / C / R&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Notes Unlocked&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What Broke &amp;amp; What Fixed It&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pre-flight probe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;0 s&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;kInputUnavailable&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;CameraSelection.front&lt;/code&gt; failed on Windows; &lt;code&gt;checkDeviceReadiness()&lt;/code&gt; tore down sessions for 30 s. Switched directly to &lt;code&gt;CameraSelection.default&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;.byId()&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;~7 s&lt;/code&gt; lock at &lt;code&gt;29–31 Hz&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Sitting 1&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(broken pipeline)&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;151.4 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt; blink cuts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Froze at &lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt; on startup (&lt;code&gt;67%&lt;/code&gt; after clearing)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;100% Center&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;0.486–0.493&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;15/15&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;30 Hz &lt;code&gt;availableCameras()&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;validationStatus&lt;/code&gt; storm starved React; 1-frame startup &lt;code&gt;face.talking&lt;/code&gt; froze &lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;0.7*iris + 0.3*yaw&lt;/code&gt; pinned gaze at Center.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Sitting 2&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(silent calibrated)&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;205.5 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;366&lt;/code&gt; keyframes (&lt;code&gt;308&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;breathRate&lt;/code&gt; msgs)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;63%&lt;/code&gt; 5-plate avg (&lt;code&gt;63.9%&lt;/code&gt; trace mean, &lt;code&gt;37–85%&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;91&lt;/code&gt; Left / &lt;code&gt;235&lt;/code&gt; Center / &lt;code&gt;40&lt;/code&gt; Right&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;11/15&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;3,3,1,1,3&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cached camera list, deduplicated status broadcasts, &lt;code&gt;≥ 5&lt;/code&gt;-frame talking guard, OLS detrending, additive iris+yaw deviation (&lt;code&gt;0.95 / 0.55&lt;/code&gt;). &lt;code&gt;26&lt;/code&gt; raw blinks → &lt;code&gt;11&lt;/code&gt; early ripples + &lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt; cuts.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Solar Coral rehearsal&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(dark theme)&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;194.7 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt; blink cuts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;57%&lt;/code&gt; 5-plate avg (stalled wave on II–IV)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Mixed L / C / R on Plate V&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;2/15&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;0,0,0,0,2&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Chest tracking dropped on Plates II–IV; drew honest dashed flatlines instead of fake curves while validating dark Solar Coral styling.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Sitting 3&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;(narrated demo capture, exported above)&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;239.2 s&lt;/code&gt; essay / &lt;code&gt;352.4 s&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;670&lt;/code&gt; keyframes&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;9,827&lt;/code&gt; 30 Hz msgs at &lt;code&gt;29.5 fps&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;523&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;breathRate&lt;/code&gt; msgs)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;72%&lt;/code&gt; 5-plate avg&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;72.4%&lt;/code&gt; trace mean, &lt;code&gt;45–89%&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;171&lt;/code&gt; Left / &lt;code&gt;406&lt;/code&gt; Center / &lt;code&gt;93&lt;/code&gt; Right&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;15/15&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; + opt-in &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;75.4 bpm&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;71.8 / 77.1 / 77.2&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Proven live: &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;807/807&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; talking-guard freeze checks across &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; speaking episodes (&lt;code&gt;57&lt;/code&gt; talking keyframes, &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; violations), &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;64&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; raw blinks (&lt;code&gt;30&lt;/code&gt; early + &lt;code&gt;34&lt;/code&gt; armed across &lt;code&gt;352.4 s&lt;/code&gt;), opt-in pulse honestly &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 40%&lt;/code&gt; on Plates I &amp;amp; V, and &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; long-blink pauses exposing the &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;42 ms&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; eyelid-descent race (&lt;code&gt;dt = 289.947 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ear = 0.213&lt;/code&gt;, fixed + Test #21).&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Comparing the earlier Contact Sheets side-by-side makes each calibration step concrete—first Sitting 1 trapped in 100% cobalt &lt;code&gt;CENTER&lt;/code&gt;, then Sitting 2 unlocking multi-zone &lt;code&gt;L / C / R&lt;/code&gt; gaze (&lt;code&gt;91 / 235 / 40&lt;/code&gt;) while staying honest about two wavering breath plates (&lt;code&gt;1/3&lt;/code&gt; on Plates III–IV), before Sitting 3 in Demo above:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fgwu2n6gdhalnyp12cod2.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fgwu2n6gdhalnyp12cod2.png" alt="Sitting 1 Contact Sheet showing 151.4s sitting and 100% solid cobalt Center gaze bars across all five plates prior to additive iris+yaw fix" width="799" height="459"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Sitting 1 (&lt;code&gt;151.4 s&lt;/code&gt;): Blinks and chest breath worked once past the startup freeze, but &lt;code&gt;0.7 * iris + 0.3 * yaw&lt;/code&gt; trapped &lt;code&gt;gazeScalar&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;[0.486..0.493]&lt;/code&gt;—100% Center across all five plates.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F4qzdw88gzw8wg1j52uop.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F4qzdw88gzw8wg1j52uop.png" alt="Sitting 2 Contact Sheet showing 205.5s silent capture, 63% breath clarity, first multi-zone L/C/R bars, and honest 11/15 notes" width="799" height="459"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Sitting 2 (&lt;code&gt;205.5 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;366&lt;/code&gt; silent keyframes): Additive iris+yaw (&lt;code&gt;0.95 / 0.55&lt;/code&gt;) unlocked Left/Center/Right bars (&lt;code&gt;91 / 235 / 40&lt;/code&gt;), Plates III–IV honestly read &lt;code&gt;1/3&lt;/code&gt; notes during unsteady breath beats (&lt;code&gt;11/15&lt;/code&gt; total), and &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; stayed OFF.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


What Real Windows Runs Taught Me
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Full technical log of all 10 hardware/SDK measurements: &lt;a href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev/blob/main/docs/SDK-NOTES.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;docs/SDK-NOTES.md&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Windows lied about the camera, and &lt;code&gt;checkDeviceReadiness()&lt;/code&gt; stalled for 30 s.&lt;/strong&gt; Windows MediaFoundation reports integrated laptop cameras (&lt;code&gt;USB\VID_13D3&amp;amp;PID_5415&lt;/code&gt;) with &lt;code&gt;facing="unknown"&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;lensType="unknown"&lt;/code&gt;, so &lt;code&gt;CameraSelection.front&lt;/code&gt; fails immediately with &lt;code&gt;kInputUnavailable&lt;/code&gt;. Calling &lt;code&gt;sdk.checkDeviceReadiness()&lt;/code&gt; also tears down any active session and waits 30 seconds on &lt;code&gt;reference720p30('full')&lt;/code&gt;. Launching &lt;code&gt;CameraSelection.default&lt;/code&gt; directly at &lt;code&gt;960×540 @ 30fps&lt;/code&gt; locks at &lt;code&gt;29–31 Hz&lt;/code&gt; in ~7 seconds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Landmarks arrived in raw pixels (&lt;code&gt;[316..564, 10..350]&lt;/code&gt;), not &lt;code&gt;[0..1]&lt;/code&gt;, so blinks and glances needed local geometry.&lt;/strong&gt; Unlike browser MediaPipe builds, &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk&lt;/code&gt; outputs all 478 landmarks (including iris centers &lt;code&gt;468&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;473&lt;/code&gt;) in raw frame pixels—which also explains why &lt;a href="https://dev.to/timothy_akanbi/long-exposure-a-daguerreotype-that-takes-a-minute-because-the-sdk-does-113l"&gt;&lt;code&gt;timothy_akanbi&lt;/code&gt;'s &lt;em&gt;Long Exposure&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; found raw blink flags and coordinates tricky for blinks. Dividing eyelid gap by eye-corner width puts open eyes cleanly at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;ear ≈ 0.298–0.313&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 0.21&lt;/code&gt; closed) and triggering cuts &lt;strong&gt;on reopen&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 650 ms&lt;/code&gt;) avoids firing when someone closes their eyes (&lt;code&gt;≥ 1.1 s&lt;/code&gt;) to pause. Replacing &lt;code&gt;0.7 * iris + 0.3 * yaw&lt;/code&gt; with additive deviation around center (&lt;code&gt;0.5 + irisDelta * 0.95 + yawDelta * 0.55&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 0.455 / &amp;gt; 0.545&lt;/code&gt;) immediately turned Sitting 1's 100%-Center wall into mixed L/C/R gaze splits (&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;91 / 235 / 40&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in Sitting 2; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;171 / 406 / 93&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in Sitting 3).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Auto-exposure collapsed brightness, dragging chest breathing across &lt;code&gt;[-6.842..+3.256]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; When USB camera drivers lack manual AE lock, SmartSpectra logs &lt;code&gt;mediafoundation_camera_source.cc:3019 [exposure-topup] lock collapsed image brightness (luma=18.8254 vs pre-lock 81.3485) ... exposure reverted to AUTO&lt;/code&gt;. That auto-exposure drift plus subtle posture lean sends &lt;code&gt;breathing.upperTrace&lt;/code&gt; sliding down a 10-unit ramp, and &lt;code&gt;upperTrace.stable&lt;/code&gt; stays &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; for ~20 s waiting on &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt;. Fitting a rolling &lt;code&gt;4.5 s&lt;/code&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) linear detrend&lt;/strong&gt; and scoring 2nd-difference curvature RMS directly responds within ~3 seconds while preserving &lt;code&gt;breathPhase&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A 30 Hz status storm and a 1-frame startup flicker froze Sitting 1.&lt;/strong&gt; Like &lt;a href="https://dev.to/samarth_kumble_a91ad88634/practical-a-webcam-physiology-lab-that-grades-itself-against-a-wrist-count-3adp"&gt;&lt;code&gt;samarth_kumble&lt;/code&gt;'s &lt;em&gt;Practical&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; noticed on Windows, &lt;code&gt;validationStatus&lt;/code&gt; fires on every single video frame (~25–30×/sec) even while &lt;code&gt;kOk&lt;/code&gt; never changes—and calling &lt;code&gt;SmartSpectraSDK.availableCameras()&lt;/code&gt; inside the status builder triggered &lt;strong&gt;30 MediaFoundation enumerations/sec&lt;/strong&gt; alongside 60 Hz SVG blur renders, while one stray &lt;code&gt;face.talking: true&lt;/code&gt; packet froze breath warmup at &lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt; and downward laptop angles read &lt;code&gt;SAD: 64.1%–97.6%&lt;/code&gt; at rest. Caching cameras, deduplicating &lt;code&gt;(validation, validationHint)&lt;/code&gt;, throttling UI updates to &lt;code&gt;~12.5 Hz&lt;/code&gt;, gating talking on &lt;code&gt;5&lt;/code&gt; consecutive frames, and smoothing &lt;code&gt;heavy&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;≥ 86%&lt;/code&gt; cured all three.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Recording my demo sitting caught one more bug (the 42 ms eyelid-descent race)—and proved the talking guard and pulse gate live.&lt;/strong&gt; Speaking on camera across &lt;strong&gt;Sitting 3&lt;/strong&gt; proved the speech guard end-to-end: across &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;15&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; speaking episodes (&lt;code&gt;822&lt;/code&gt; talking packets at &lt;code&gt;29.5 fps&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;57&lt;/code&gt; keyframes in &lt;code&gt;sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;breathSteadiness&lt;/code&gt; stayed locked across &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;807 / 807&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; consecutive talking checks with &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; violations. Opt-in &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; also behaved honestly once flipped ON mid-sitting (&lt;code&gt;dt = 264.6 s&lt;/code&gt;): Plates II–IV printed &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;71.8 / 77.1 / 77.2 bpm&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;75.4 bpm&lt;/code&gt; avg), while Plate I (pre-toggle) and Plate V (extreme left gaze pushing rPPG confidence &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 40%&lt;/code&gt;) stayed suppressed (&lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;). Out of &lt;code&gt;4&lt;/code&gt; long-blink pauses (&lt;code&gt;157.86 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;259.14 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;291.11 s&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;320.69 s&lt;/code&gt;), pause #3 exposed one subtle race: native &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; fired at &lt;code&gt;dt = 289.947 s&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;ear = 0.213&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;0.003&lt;/code&gt; above the &lt;code&gt;0.21&lt;/code&gt; closure cutoff) &lt;strong&gt;42 ms before&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;ear&lt;/code&gt; dropped to &lt;code&gt;0.175&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;289.989 s&lt;/code&gt; for a &lt;code&gt;2.44 s&lt;/code&gt; hold. Gating native &lt;code&gt;face.blinking&lt;/code&gt; fallback on &lt;code&gt;lastEar &amp;gt;= 0.25&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;nativeBlinkEarFloor&lt;/code&gt;) eliminates descent misfires without breaking partial-blink fallback, locked in by &lt;strong&gt;Regression Test #21&lt;/strong&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Excerpt from bridge/signal-processor.mjs — native blinking descent guard (Test #21)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nativeEarClear&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;lastEar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;lastEar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;nativeBlinkEarFloor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;wasLowEar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nativeEarClear&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;longBlinkFired&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;closedElapsed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;blinkCut&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Honest Limits
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Single person, single laptop (&lt;code&gt;n = 1&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; Every live sitting and threshold in this post was calibrated on me in front of one Windows x64 laptop webcam in indoor lighting; it has not yet been tested on macOS/Linux or across Fitzpatrick V–VI skin tones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No packet capture on Presage's §7.4 gateway:&lt;/strong&gt; The Consent section below states strictly what Presage's SDK 3.5.0 source code and docs specify rather than claiming a wire-level network audit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Prize Categories
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I am entering &lt;strong&gt;Most Creative or Delightful Use&lt;/strong&gt; (in addition to Overall consideration):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Directly inspired by &lt;a href="https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0004555/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Walter Murch&lt;/strong&gt;'s&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Blink_of_an_Eye_%28book%29" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the Blink of an Eye&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://www.imdb.com/title/tt15575678/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Before Your Eyes&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;AFTERIMAGE&lt;/strong&gt; turns contactless webcam sensing from a vitals chart into slow darkroom cinema: an eye glance shifts panel sharpness and stereo WebAudio harmonies, calm chest breathing clears SVG optical haze to wake hidden italic marginalia (&lt;code&gt;15/15&lt;/code&gt; unlocked on Sitting 3, honestly stalling to dashed flatlines when signal drops), a &lt;code&gt;4.2 s&lt;/code&gt; dwell gate turns ordinary blinks from nuisance triggers into deliberate film cuts (&lt;code&gt;30&lt;/code&gt; reading blinks absorbed cleanly so &lt;code&gt;34&lt;/code&gt; intentional cuts told the story), and the sitting ends by printing an honest &lt;code&gt;1600×920&lt;/code&gt; Contact Sheet you can download or erase in one click.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Consent and Data Handling
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Camera stays off until explicit consent:&lt;/strong&gt; Video capture never starts on load. On &lt;code&gt;/calibrate&lt;/code&gt;, Live Bridge mode requires checking consent and clicking to start; closing or navigating away stops capture cleanly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No raw video or audio stored:&lt;/strong&gt; Native Node decodes camera frames locally at &lt;code&gt;960×540 @ 30fps&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;127.0.0.1:4199&lt;/code&gt; and discards them from RAM immediately. Only normalized &lt;code&gt;[0..1]&lt;/code&gt; geometric silhouette vectors and scalar blink/gaze/breath values traverse localhost WebSocket. Microphone permission is never requested.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SDK telemetry OFF &amp;amp; &lt;code&gt;requestInsight()&lt;/code&gt; never called:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/emarc99/presage-dev/blob/main/bridge/server.mjs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bridge/server.mjs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; constructs every SDK instance with &lt;code&gt;enableTelemetry: false&lt;/code&gt; and never calls &lt;code&gt;sdk.requestInsight()&lt;/code&gt;. Both invariants are asserted on every CI push in &lt;code&gt;npm test&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;npm run verify-trace&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Accurate Presage §7.4 LLM Insights disclosure:&lt;/strong&gt; Leaving &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; &lt;strong&gt;OFF by default&lt;/strong&gt; requests only &lt;code&gt;faceMetrics + breathingMetrics&lt;/code&gt;, so pulse and HRV are never computed or buffered. However, inspection of Presage's &lt;a href="https://smartspectra.presagetech.com/docs/llm-insights" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;LLM Insights docs&lt;/a&gt;, Privacy Policy §7.4, and &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk@3.5.0&lt;/code&gt; source (&lt;code&gt;_ensureSession()&lt;/code&gt; registers &lt;code&gt;onInsight&lt;/code&gt; unconditionally) shows that when &lt;code&gt;breathing.rate&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;cardio&lt;/code&gt; when enabled) is active, the SDK automatically dispatches short derived numeric series (never raw video) to Presage's Analytics Gateway / Anthropic LLM service and cannot currently be turned off by developers. AFTERIMAGE discloses this plainly upfront on &lt;code&gt;/calibrate&lt;/code&gt;, never requests or displays AI insights, and warns inline before opt-in &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; is switched ON (plus suppressing &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 40%&lt;/code&gt; confidence pulse readings due to camera rPPG sensitivity in dim lighting and Fitzpatrick V–VI skin tones).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Opt-in trace recording &amp;amp; one-click erasure:&lt;/strong&gt; Local trace recording (&lt;code&gt;.jsonl&lt;/code&gt; inside gitignored &lt;code&gt;recordings/&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;web/public/sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;) runs only when explicitly invoked, and &lt;code&gt;/contact-sheet&lt;/code&gt; provides one-click in-memory erasure (&lt;code&gt;Erase Session Data&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Non-medical notice:&lt;/strong&gt; AFTERIMAGE is an interactive digital art and narrative experiment for creative and informational purposes only; it is not a medical device and makes no diagnosis or treatment claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Agent Session
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Built with &lt;strong&gt;Antigravity&lt;/strong&gt; as my AI coding agent and pair programmer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sitting 1's &lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt; freeze and 100%-Center diagnosis through the additive gaze fix and Sitting 2 breakthrough:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="ltag-agent-session"&gt;
&lt;div class="agent-session-header"&gt;

&lt;span class="agent-session-tool-icon-badge" title="Gemini CLI"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="agent-session-title"&gt;Building AFTERIMAGE: steering a memory essay with SmartSpectra blinks, gaze, and chest breath&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="agent-session-scroll"&gt;

&lt;div class="agent-session-message agent-session-user"&gt;
&lt;div class="agent-session-role-badge agent-session-role-user"&gt;
You
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="agent-session-content"&gt;
&lt;div class="agent-session-text"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;step 1, number 1, what am I doing on this page?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"Scene I of V · Morning Steam&lt;br&gt;
Kitchen table · 06:14 AM · Beat 1/3&lt;br&gt;
DEVELOPING · 55%&lt;br&gt;
Sound: On&lt;br&gt;
Signals Info&lt;br&gt;
FOCUS: Ceramic Cup&lt;br&gt;
TALKING · BREATH HELD&lt;br&gt;
SHUTTER ARMED · BLINK TO CUT&lt;br&gt;
Steam still curls off the dark surface untouched since six.&lt;br&gt;
First light slips between the blind slats onto an empty kitchen table. Nobody has spoken yet; the kettle only stopped whistling a minute ago.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hold steady breathing (≥ 60%) to clear haze and develop the hidden marginalia.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Blink Cut · Space&lt;br&gt;
GAZE&lt;br&gt;
left&lt;br&gt;
center&lt;br&gt;
right&lt;br&gt;
Pause&lt;br&gt;
BREATH&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;55%&lt;br&gt;
Finish Roll → Contact Sheet"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="agent-session-message agent-session-assistant"&gt;
&lt;div class="agent-session-role-badge agent-session-role-assistant"&gt;
Agent
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="agent-session-content"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class="agent-session-text agent-session-text-collapse"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You're already on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;/experience&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (Step 3 — &lt;strong&gt;Scene I of V&lt;/strong&gt;), and your live SmartSpectra webcam &lt;strong&gt;is actively streaming&lt;/strong&gt; right now (&lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;TALKING · BREATH HELD&lt;/code&gt; only come from the live bridge).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-13-what-to-do-on-this-page-experience"&gt;What to Do on This Page (&lt;code&gt;/experience&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are &lt;strong&gt;3 physical interactions&lt;/strong&gt; (hands off the keyboard):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Breathe steadily (&lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;≥ 60%&lt;/code&gt;) to clear the blur &amp;amp; unlock the hidden line:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep your mouth still/quiet for ~2 seconds so &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;TALKING · BREATH HELD&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; clears (while that badge is active, your breath meter intentionally freezes at &lt;code&gt;55%&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit back slightly so your upper chest is in view and take &lt;strong&gt;2–3 slow, even breaths&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Once the badge crosses &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;≥ 60%&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;FOCUS SHARP&lt;/code&gt;), the illustration sharpens, a soft chime rings, and &lt;code&gt;"Hold steady breathing..."&lt;/code&gt; transforms into the hidden italic marginalia line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Shift your eyes Left / Center / Right:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Glance &lt;strong&gt;left&lt;/strong&gt; (venetian blinds), &lt;strong&gt;center&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;FOCUS: Ceramic Cup&lt;/code&gt;), or &lt;strong&gt;right&lt;/strong&gt; (folded napkin note). The spotlight frame, parallax, caption, and stereo audio shift to follow your gaze.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Blink once to advance (&lt;code&gt;SHUTTER ARMED · BLINK TO CUT&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Because the &lt;code&gt;4.2 s&lt;/code&gt; dwell lock is already armed, give &lt;strong&gt;one normal blink&lt;/strong&gt; to trigger the eyelid shutter cut (&lt;code&gt;Beat 1/3 → 2/3 → 3/3 → Scene II → ... → Scene V → Contact Sheet&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding your eyes shut for &lt;strong&gt;~1.2 s&lt;/strong&gt; toggles &lt;code&gt;PAUSED (LONG BLINK)&lt;/code&gt; without cutting. &lt;em&gt;(Pressing &lt;code&gt;Space&lt;/code&gt; or clicking &lt;code&gt;Blink Cut · Space&lt;/code&gt; also advances anytime.)&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-13-if-you-meant-to-do-step-1-first-pulse-toggle-test--recording"&gt;If You Meant to Do Step 1 First (Pulse Toggle Test + Recording)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Calibrate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in the top navigation bar to open &lt;code&gt;/calibrate&lt;/code&gt;. That's where:&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Optional Optical Pulse (cardioMetrics)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; switch lives (to test live BPM with the §7.4 disclosure), and&lt;br&gt;
- &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Record Sitting&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; button lives (click it right before clicking &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Enter Scene I →&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; so your sitting gets saved to &lt;code&gt;web/public/sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt; when you finish on &lt;code&gt;/contact-sheet&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;


