&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No issue at all—every single one of those lines is harmless upstream C++ stderr output from inside &lt;code&gt;@smartspectra/node-sdk&lt;/code&gt;, not an error in AFTERIMAGE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;inference_feedback_manager.cc:114&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;absl::InitializeLog()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — Standard TensorFlow Lite / MediaPipe startup noise inside Presage's native addon whenever an SDK session starts (it printed twice in your second run because you started/restarted capture twice: timestamps &lt;code&gt;...4237&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;...4520&lt;/code&gt;). Completely normal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;landmark_projection_calculator.cc:78&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — Standard internal MediaPipe FaceMesh graph warning inside the native SDK; cannot be silenced from JS and has zero effect on tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;mediafoundation_camera_source.cc:3019 [exposure-topup] ... exposure reverted to AUTO&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — Hardware-specific safe fallback on your integrated laptop camera driver:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SmartSpectra tries to lock Auto-Exposure (AE) at startup; your laptop USB webcam driver has no manual gain/AE lock, so brightness collapsed (&lt;code&gt;luma 81.3 → 18.8&lt;/code&gt;) and the SDK automatically recovered by reverting to &lt;code&gt;AUTO&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zero problem for blinks, gaze, or chest breathing&lt;/strong&gt; (and our OLS linear detrending in &lt;code&gt;signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt; already absorbs slow auto-exposure drift).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Good engineering note for your DEV post:&lt;/strong&gt; Because laptop webcams without AE lock make rPPG pulse noisier, this hardware behavior actually &lt;em&gt;validates&lt;/em&gt; why AFTERIMAGE builds core interaction on face + chest breathing and keeps &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; opt-in &amp;amp; confidence-gated (&lt;code&gt;&amp;gt;= 40%&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Quick check on the two items from your run so we know whether to tune anything before your recorded sitting + Vercel deploy:&lt;br&gt;
1. &lt;strong&gt;Gaze L / C / R:&lt;/strong&gt; Did you try glancing left/right and find it stuck on &lt;code&gt;CENTER&lt;/code&gt; (want me to tighten &lt;code&gt;0.41 / 0.59&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;0.45 / 0.55&lt;/code&gt;)?&lt;br&gt;
2. &lt;strong&gt;Opt-in Pulse (&lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; Did toggling it ON on &lt;code&gt;/calibrate&lt;/code&gt; show a live BPM reading, or did it stay &lt;code&gt;warming up&lt;/code&gt; under auto-exposure?&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Great—knowing the live BPM readout worked confirms the opt-in &lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt; path end to end, and tightening gaze addresses why the L/C/R bar stayed all-center.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-19-fixed--pushed-128558a"&gt;Fixed &amp;amp; Pushed (&lt;code&gt;128558a&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;bridge/signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replaced the averaged &lt;code&gt;computeGazeScalar&lt;/code&gt; blend (&lt;code&gt;irisRatio * 0.7 + yawRatio * 0.3&lt;/code&gt;) with additive deviation fusion around center (&lt;code&gt;0.5 + (irisRatio - 0.5) * 0.95 + (yawRatio - 0.5) * 0.55&lt;/code&gt;) so eye glances and natural head movement amplify rather than dilute each other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tightened 3-zone thresholds from &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 0.41 / &amp;gt; 0.59&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;0.46 / 0.54&lt;/code&gt; return) to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt; 0.455 / &amp;gt; 0.545&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;0.478 / 0.522&lt;/code&gt; return), staying outside resting jitter (&lt;code&gt;~0.486–0.493&lt;/code&gt;) while responding to gentle glances across a laptop screen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;bridge/signal-processor.test.mjs&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Added subtle-glance (&lt;code&gt;gazeOffset = ±0.25&lt;/code&gt;) assertions across &lt;code&gt;left&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;right&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;code&gt;center&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Checks after final edit:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;node --check bridge/signal-processor.mjs&lt;/code&gt; exited &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;npm test&lt;/code&gt; passed &lt;strong&gt;9/9&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;114.47 ms&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-19-your-final-capture-pass-recorded-sitting--demo-video-together"&gt;Your Final Capture Pass (Recorded Sitting + Demo Video Together)&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Restart &lt;code&gt;npm start&lt;/code&gt; once (&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+C&lt;/code&gt;, then &lt;code&gt;npm start&lt;/code&gt;) so Node picks up the new gaze thresholds, then do one pass at &lt;code&gt;http://&lt;span class="agent-session-redacted"&gt;[REDACTED]&lt;/span&gt;:4199&lt;/code&gt; &lt;em&gt;(start your screen + webcam PiP recording now if you want your 60–90 s challenge demo video from the exact same sitting)&lt;/em&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;On &lt;code&gt;/calibrate&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;em&gt;(Optional for video)&lt;/em&gt; Toggle &lt;strong&gt;Optional Optical Pulse (&lt;code&gt;cardioMetrics&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt; ON for a few seconds to show live BPM + the §7.4 disclosure, then toggle it back &lt;strong&gt;OFF&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Record Sitting&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (confirm it changes to &lt;code&gt;Stop &amp;amp; Save Sample (N)&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Enter Scene I →&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Across &lt;code&gt;/experience&lt;/code&gt; (Scenes I → V):&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look &lt;strong&gt;Left&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Center&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Right&lt;/strong&gt; across each scene's panes so the triptych spotlight shifts cleanly and paints a real 3-color L / C / R bar on your Contact Sheet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Breathe calmly past &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;60%&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;FOCUS SHARP&lt;/code&gt;) and blink after &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;SHUTTER ARMED&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;4.2 s&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;On &lt;code&gt;/contact-sheet&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Save Recording → sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in the green banner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Download Print (.png)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tell me once you save the recording and confirm how L/C/R gaze feels—next up I'll commit your real &lt;code&gt;sample-trace.json&lt;/code&gt;, run &lt;code&gt;npm run build&lt;/code&gt;, deploy to Vercel (&lt;code&gt;vercel --prod&lt;/code&gt;), and draft your &lt;code&gt;#presagechallenge&lt;/code&gt; DEV submission post.&lt;/p&gt;

