&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-7-1-live-smartspectra-spike-results"&gt;1. Live SmartSpectra Spike Results&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your &lt;code&gt;SMARTSPECTRA_API_KEY&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; authenticated cleanly on Windows x64 + &lt;code&gt;Node v24.9.0&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;Integrated Camera&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;960×540 @ 30fps&lt;/code&gt;) and zero DLL/auth errors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two concrete SDK findings shaped the bridge:

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calling &lt;code&gt;stopAsync()&lt;/code&gt; alone kept Node open until &lt;code&gt;sdk.destroy()&lt;/code&gt; ran (&lt;code&gt;d0f441e&lt;/code&gt; fixed both &lt;code&gt;spike/camera-spike.mjs&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;bridge/server.mjs&lt;/code&gt;, adding &lt;code&gt;--skip-readiness&lt;/code&gt; so camera startup never blocks 30s on &lt;code&gt;checkDeviceReadiness()&lt;/code&gt; timeouts).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;During the background spike runs, the camera reported &lt;code&gt;kNoFaceFound (No face found.)&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;lm=0&lt;/code&gt;) because nobody was framed in front of an uncovered lens—so &lt;strong&gt;you should still run a live 15-second seated check once&lt;/strong&gt; before recording your demo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h3 id="agent-session-1410-7-2-atomic-commits-pushed-d0f441e7c864c3"&gt;2. Atomic Commits Pushed (&lt;code&gt;d0f441e..7c864c3&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/h3&gt;

